    "Notes Updated": "10/2/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Big extension and a funky delivery\n 4FB has jumped in velo, now sitting around 95 and has topped at 99, plays extremely well at the top of the zone due to  4.3 VAA\n Throws his 2FB a ton too, not as good a pitch, averages 2 MPH less than the 4FB and it hasn't performed super well. I'd use this less if I were him / the Brewers.\n Slider is a sweeper that he didn't command as well this year, but still gets a solid whiff rate against it\n Curveball is actually a pitch I like quite a bit, but I think he's dropping his arm too much and telegraphing it\n I would use the changeup more, but he does need to improve the command of it for that to work\n Does a great job limiting walks, but could use refinement within the zone with his command.\n Has a lot more velo than most guys throwing from his slot, with a funky delivery.\n He has fallen off a bit, due to some struggles in Nashville, but still a very interesting bullpen arm",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/20/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Reliever\n Indy Ball signing this year in June\n Moving very quickly through the system.\n Tough side arm angle\n Shows a low 90's fastball that he can use up in the zone.\n Throws a changeup that is decent looking.\n Slider is his best pitch. Get's a lot of sweep and generates a lot of whiffs.\n Command is good, can nibble at times and cause some walks.\n Has a little more velo than most guys throwing from his slot, with a funky delivery.\n Brewers seem to like him a lot, moving him quickly\nUPDATE as of 10/12:\n Pitching in the AFL, getting some statcast data. Slider being classified as a curve. Not sure I'd agree. Getting a lot of movement. \n Spin rates aren't anything to be too excited about but appear to be pretty good for a low slot guy like he is.",
